  "basis": "The chart visually encodes population using color: orange for 30+ million, purple for 20-30 million. California and Texas are both orange (30+ M), while Florida is purple (20-30 M). The routing policy requires selecting the single highest-population state from the offered options. Since California and Texas share the same top population bin (30+ M), the chart does not provide sufficient evidence to distinguish one as definitively higher than the other. Therefore, no option can be uniquely justified as the 'highest-population' state based on this visualization alone.",
